They're definitely not, they're not responsive to how you're actually jumping in the real world.

00:16:28.660 --> 00:16:33.660
Yeah. They, you know, they hang up as long as you're hung up, but there is like more of a, it's

00:16:33.660 --> 00:16:34.740
like a lunge to it.

00:16:34.740 --> 00:16:36.460
I don't know. It just bothered me that it wasn't.

00:16:36.480 --> 00:16:39.760
Well, I think it's more because, um, it's a binary.

00:16:40.360 --> 00:16:46.280
Um, it's a binary of either you are on the ground or you are like three feet up in the

00:16:46.280 --> 00:16:51.940
air. So it looks weird, but I think that in order for the game to work in, like when you're

00:16:51.940 --> 00:16:54.420
playing it physically, it sort of has to do that.

00:16:55.020 --> 00:16:55.940
I don't know.

00:16:56.340 --> 00:17:00.060
