Um, rhythm games can be good.

00:28:12.880 --> 00:28:14.240
I want to state... I want to just state that.

00:28:14.320 --> 00:28:15.300
Rhythm games can be good.

00:28:15.960 --> 00:28:18.300
Games that use gimmicks can be good.

00:28:18.460 --> 00:28:24.940
There are many good Wii games that are just not playable today if you don't have the Wii

00:28:24.940 --> 00:28:30.120
mode. Like, you can't just be, like, Switch port when, because they'd have to redesign the game.

00:28:30.160 --> 00:28:34.500
I think one that's really guilty of that is Skyward Sword, but I don't think that's a great

00:28:34.500 --> 00:28:36.120
one, necessarily. It's not a great game.

00:28:36.260 --> 00:28:38.120
Is it a hot take? It's...

00:28:38.560 --> 00:28:39.800
Uh, I think it's kind of a hot take.

00:28:39.920 --> 00:28:41.980
I think people have started to realize, like, when that game came out...

00:28:41.980 --> 00:28:43.400
The hive mind has started to sway.

00:28:43.560 --> 00:28:47.860
Yeah. When that game came out, people were giving it tens, and everybody got very excited.

00:28:47.860 --> 00:28:53.220
And I think tens are crazy for a game like that, because you constantly are getting tutorials

00:28:53.220 --> 00:28:54.240
for the entire game.

00:28:54.240 --> 00:28:59.000
Even on things like rupees, as you pick them up, every time you start the game save file,

00:28:59.200 --> 00:29:02.500
it reminds you what a rupee is the first time you pick it up in each time you start

00:29:02.500 --> 00:29:03.520
up the game. Dear God.

00:29:03.700 --> 00:29:06.100
Crazy. So, things like this, I don't know.

00:29:06.200 --> 00:29:11.460
I just don't... Something about, like, the nature of these games, it just doesn't jive well with me.

00:29:11.580 --> 00:29:13.620
And so, stadium events.

00:29:14.240 --> 00:29:16.020
